{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write batches of records for PostHog’s batch capture API, for an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to send."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder"},{"text":" is the ","type":"text"},{"code":"BatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for PostHog Cloud’s or a self-hosted PostHog’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/batch\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Give it to an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"text":") as its encoder, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"your instance’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/batch\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" URL. The project token goes in the body, so no header field is needed.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes an anonymous event. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session, from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sessions enricher, also sent as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a record with no session is sent under its own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record identifier. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"uuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event carries ","type":"text"},{"code":"$process_person_profile: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$geoip_disable: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The record’s vendor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier and trace context aren’t sent, and the standard context is sent as PostHog’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties (","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the like).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals, and a property whose name starts with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or is ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is left out and logged. A record the encoder can’t write is left out and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and one holding a value JSON can’t.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batch(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns each as a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogSkippedRecord","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to TraffluentCollector, use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","import Instrumentation","import PostHogEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = TrackingPlan(schemas: [SignedUp.schema, SessionStarted.schema, SessionEnded.schema])","let encoder = PostHogBatchEncoder(projectToken: projectToken, plan: plan)","let postHog = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: postHogBatchURL,  \/\/ https:\/\/us.i.posthog.com\/batch\/, https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com\/batch\/ or your own","    instrument: NoOpInstrument(),  \/\/ so no trace context goes to PostHog in the header fields","    encoder: encoder)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: postHog)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what PostHog receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatch"],"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogSkippedRecord","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","interfaceL